es only with the 1.3 liter petrol  engine  but a man will points out that you can  choose from two transmissions a  six-speed manual or a continuously  variable transmission CVT the Honda Jazz  can go from 0 to 100 km/h in just over  11 seconds it can reach a top speed of  190 km/h and as far as fuel efficiency  is concerned the Jazz gets 100  kilometers on 5 liters of gas in Poltava  the manual says the Jazz handles pretty  well on the road and it holds the line  comfortably through corners the engines  a little low on torque so it takes you a  while to notice the change after you  shifted gears missing from 40 back  overall a manual has mixed feelings  about the Honda Jazz its design reminds  him a lot of the Civic but that's just a  matter of personal taste a motor the  engines not very powerful particularly  under 3,000 rpm Velen doc but the Jazz  is pretty right whether you're sitting  in the back seat or eluding a bunch of  stuff into the trunk and you can even  have more space by reconfiguring the  seats that's one of the cars big  advantages  the price for the Honda Jazz in Germany  is just under 16 thousand euros and if  you include all the options that we did  in our test model plus a few extras the  price could easily top twenty thousand  you
 

